With Apple's upcoming iPhone Ultra there's been a lingering question over the exact placement of the selfie cameras in the device's folded and unfolded states – but today we may have stumbled upon the answer. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/foldable-iphone-dummy-sonny-dickson.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1050898" /><br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/06/07/best-look-yet-at-foldable-iphone-design-revealed/">Dummy units</a> have suggested a top-centered cut-out for the selfie camera on the outer display of Apple's foldable, while locating the selfie camera for the inner display in the outermost top-left corner. That presents an asymmetry untypical of Apple's designs.<br/>
<br/>
However, screen protectors for the iPhone Ultra that <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/12/iphone-ultra-screen-protectors-reveal-asymmetry/">surfaced online today</a> suggest the device's selfie cameras on the inner and outer displays may be located in the same corner of the same half, with one facing out and one facing in.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/dummy-iphone-ultra-open-sonny.jpg" alt="" width="1154" height="930" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059402" /><br/>
The screen protectors show a selfie camera cutout on the top-right corner of the outer display when the device is closed. Taken together, the two leaks could imply one front-facing camera zone in a single corner.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/foldable-iphone-screen-protectors.jpg" alt="" width="1440" height="1030" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059400" /><br/>
Such an arrangement – two slightly offset lenses – could let Apple confine the cutouts and camera modules to a single region of a 4.5mm thick chassis, rather than having them spaced out in different places, which would fit for a device where internal space is at a premium. <br/>
<br/>
Now, accessory makers typically work from leaked CAD files of sometimes dubious accuracy, so a pair of screen protectors can't be considered to provide definitive evidence of a device's design. Our reading also assumes the dummy iPhone Ultra models had one camera placement correct (the top-left inner selfie camera) and one out of whack (the centered outer camera). Even so, the side-by-side internal placement could make sense.<br/>
<br/>
